WEBVTT

00:00:00.492 --> 00:00:03.344
Oxford Bookworms, stage 1.

00:00:03.404 --> 00:00:13.703
The Elephant Man by Tim Vickery, published by Oxford University Press, chapter 1, The Creature in the Shop.

00:00:13.763 --> 00:00:18.166
My name is Dr. Frederick Treves.

00:00:18.226 --> 00:00:21.419
I am a doctor at the London Hospital.

00:00:21.479 --> 00:00:29.274
One day, in 1884, I saw a picture in the window of a shop near the hospital.

00:00:29.334 --> 00:00:34.036
I stopped in front of the shop and looked at the picture.

00:00:34.096 --> 00:00:36.998
At first I felt interested.

00:00:37.058 --> 00:00:39.130
Then I felt angry.

00:00:39.190 --> 00:00:41.012
Then afraid.

00:00:41.072 --> 00:00:44.534
It was a horrible, ugly picture.

00:00:44.594 --> 00:00:50.138
There was a man in the picture, but he did not look like you and me.

00:00:50.198 --> 00:00:52.792
He did not look like a man.

00:00:52.852 --> 00:00:55.614
He looked like an elephant.

00:00:55.674 --> 00:00:58.954
I read the writing under the picture.

00:00:59.014 --> 00:01:05.066
It said, come in and see the elephant man, two pence.

00:01:05.126 --> 00:01:08.388
I opened the door and went in.

00:01:08.448 --> 00:01:11.229
There was a man in the shop.

00:01:11.289 --> 00:01:16.932
He was a dirty man in an old coat with a cigarette in his mouth.

00:01:16.992 --> 00:01:19.072
What do you want?

00:01:19.133 --> 00:01:20.804
He asked.

00:01:20.864 --> 00:01:25.556
I'd like to see the elephant man, please, I said.

00:01:25.616 --> 00:01:28.690
The man looked at me angrily.

00:01:28.750 --> 00:01:31.674
Well, you can't," he said.

00:01:31.733 --> 00:01:34.256
The shop's closing now.

00:01:34.316 --> 00:01:37.028
You can come back tomorrow.

00:01:37.088 --> 00:01:39.770
I'm sorry, I said.

00:01:39.830 --> 00:01:42.461
But I would like to see him now.

00:01:42.521 --> 00:01:44.822
I have no time tomorrow.

00:01:44.882 --> 00:01:47.194
I have a lot of work to do.

00:01:47.254 --> 00:01:50.846
But I can give you more than two pens."

00:01:50.906 --> 00:01:54.320
The man looked at me carefully.

00:01:54.380 --> 00:01:57.314
Then he took the cigarette out of his mouth.

00:01:57.374 --> 00:01:59.797
and smiled with his yellow teeth.

00:01:59.817 --> 00:02:03.718
"'All right, sir,' he said.

00:02:03.738 --> 00:02:07.579
"'Give me twelve pence then.'

00:02:07.639 --> 00:02:13.291
I gave him the money, and he opened a door at the back of the shop.

00:02:13.351 --> 00:02:16.082
We went into a little room.

00:02:16.142 --> 00:02:22.124
The room was cold and dark, and there was a horrible smell in it.

00:02:22.184 --> 00:02:26.811
A creature sat on a chair behind a table.

00:02:26.870 --> 00:02:33.928
I say a creature, because it was not a man or a woman like you or me.

00:02:33.988 --> 00:02:38.370
The creature did not move or look at us.

00:02:38.430 --> 00:02:47.934
It sat very quietly on the chair in the cold, dark, dirty room and looked at the table.

00:02:47.994 --> 00:02:54.147
The creature had a cloth over its head because of the cold.

00:02:54.207 --> 00:02:58.840
On the table in front of it there was a dead flower.

00:02:58.900 --> 00:03:00.782
Stand up!"

00:03:00.842 --> 00:03:03.434
said the shopkeeper loudly.

00:03:03.493 --> 00:03:06.896
The creature stood up slowly.

00:03:06.956 --> 00:03:12.811
It took the old cloth of its head and put it on the chair.

00:03:12.870 --> 00:03:17.634
I looked at the creature and felt sad.

00:03:17.694 --> 00:03:23.788
I am a doctor, so I know a lot about accidents and ill people.

00:03:23.848 --> 00:03:27.809
I see horrible, ugly things every day.

00:03:27.869 --> 00:03:33.721
But this creature, this thing, was the worst of all.

00:03:33.781 --> 00:03:38.603
There were no men or women in the hospital like him.

00:03:38.662 --> 00:03:48.836
He wore some old trousers, but no shirt, coat, or shoes, so I could see his body very well.

00:03:48.896 --> 00:03:51.897
His head was the most interesting thing.

00:03:51.957 --> 00:03:58.770
It was very, very big, like an enormous bag with a lot of books in it.

00:03:58.830 --> 00:04:08.016
The head did not have much hair, and there was another bag of brown, dirty skin at the back of it.

00:04:08.076 --> 00:04:12.468
This skin came down below his neck.

00:04:12.528 --> 00:04:22.031
I could not see one of his eyes very well because a lot of skin came down in front of his face, too.

00:04:22.091 --> 00:04:28.362
An enormous red tooth came out of his mouth under his nose.

00:04:28.422 --> 00:04:31.626
It looked like an elephant's tooth.

00:04:31.686 --> 00:04:36.140
The mouth and nose were like holes in the face.

00:04:36.200 --> 00:04:44.646
The face could not smile or laugh or look angry or sad because the skin could not move.

00:04:44.706 --> 00:04:49.229
It was dead like an elephant's face.

00:04:49.289 --> 00:04:55.692
There were more bags of dirty skin on the front and back of the creature's body.

00:04:55.751 --> 00:04:59.334
These bags came down to his legs.

00:04:59.393 --> 00:05:05.536
The right arm was enormous, and there were bags of skin on it too.

00:05:05.596 --> 00:05:10.040
The right hand was like a man's foot.

00:05:10.100 --> 00:05:17.014
But the left hand, the left arm and the left hand, were beautiful.

00:05:17.074 --> 00:05:25.507
The left arm had wonderful skin, and the fingers of the left hand were long and beautiful.

00:05:25.567 --> 00:05:28.968
It was like a young woman's hand.

00:05:29.028 --> 00:05:31.489
Walk, Merrick!

00:05:31.549 --> 00:05:33.640
said the shopkeeper angrily.

00:05:33.700 --> 00:05:35.360
Come on, quickly!

00:05:35.420 --> 00:05:36.730
Move!

00:05:36.790 --> 00:05:39.711
He hit the creature with his hand.

00:05:39.771 --> 00:05:43.763
Slowly the creature walked across the room.

00:05:43.822 --> 00:05:46.060
But he could not walk well.

00:05:46.120 --> 00:05:50.970
His legs were very big and fat, and he had a bad back.

00:05:51.030 --> 00:05:54.352
He could not walk far without a stick.

00:05:54.412 --> 00:05:58.394
"'All right, thank you,' I said.

00:05:58.454 --> 00:06:00.165
Let him sit down.

00:06:00.224 --> 00:06:02.606
I don't want to see any more.'

00:06:02.666 --> 00:06:06.867
I felt ill, and the smell in the room was very bad.

00:06:06.887 --> 00:06:10.269
"'Yes, sir,' said the shopkeeper.

00:06:10.289 --> 00:06:13.260
"'Sit down, Merrick.'

00:06:13.319 --> 00:06:17.131
We went out of the room and closed the door.

00:06:17.191 --> 00:06:20.313
The shopkeeper smiled at me with his yellow teeth.

00:06:20.333 --> 00:06:23.926
"'Wonderful, sir, isn't it?'

00:06:23.986 --> 00:06:24.596
he said.

00:06:24.616 --> 00:06:28.189
"'The best elephant man in England.

00:06:28.248 --> 00:06:31.341
Hundreds of people come to see him, you know.

00:06:31.401 --> 00:06:32.552
Hundreds!

00:06:32.612 --> 00:06:35.164
I take him all over the country, I do.'

00:06:35.184 --> 00:06:37.276
"'Yes.

00:06:37.335 --> 00:06:39.327
Very interesting,' I said.

00:06:39.347 --> 00:06:41.088
"'Can I sit down?'

00:06:41.108 --> 00:06:42.989
"'Yes, sir.

00:06:43.049 --> 00:06:44.336
Of course.'

00:06:44.396 --> 00:06:46.523
Here's a chair!"

00:06:46.582 --> 00:06:49.105
He looked at me, smiling.

00:06:49.164 --> 00:06:52.367
Would you like a glass of water, sir?

00:06:52.426 --> 00:06:55.499
Yes, please, I said.

00:06:55.559 --> 00:06:59.252
Then I looked at the things in the dirty shop.

00:06:59.312 --> 00:07:04.376
There were two or three bad apples, and some old black bananas.

00:07:04.436 --> 00:07:06.218
That was all.

00:07:06.278 --> 00:07:08.278
Uh, no.

00:07:08.338 --> 00:07:09.800
No, thank you.

00:07:09.860 --> 00:07:13.179
I'm all right, I said.

00:07:13.238 --> 00:07:17.417
Did you call the creature Merrick?

00:07:17.477 --> 00:07:19.248
That's right, sir.

00:07:19.308 --> 00:07:24.490
Joseph Merrick, the best elephant man in England.

00:07:24.550 --> 00:07:27.501
I take him all over the country, you know.

00:07:27.561 --> 00:07:30.172
Lots of people want to see him.

00:07:30.232 --> 00:07:32.873
Yes, I see.

00:07:32.933 --> 00:07:35.274
Do you get a lot of money?

00:07:35.334 --> 00:07:38.315
Well, sometimes we do, sir.

00:07:38.375 --> 00:07:39.576
Yes.

00:07:39.636 --> 00:07:44.271
But it's difficult, you see, sir, because of the police.

00:07:44.331 --> 00:07:47.667
The police don't like us, you see, sir.

00:07:47.727 --> 00:07:51.440
So we can't stay in a town very long.

00:07:51.499 --> 00:07:54.382
We usually move every week.

00:07:54.442 --> 00:07:57.164
Yes, I see.

00:07:57.224 --> 00:08:02.496
Well, anyway, Mr. uh, Silcox, sir.

00:08:02.556 --> 00:08:05.038
Simon, Silcox?

00:08:05.098 --> 00:08:07.830
Yes, well, Mr. Silcox.

00:08:07.890 --> 00:08:11.102
I'm a doctor at the London hospital.

00:08:11.162 --> 00:08:13.905
My name is Dr. Treves.

00:08:13.964 --> 00:08:24.299
I think this, uh, this man, Joseph Merrick, is very interesting, and I would like to see him at the hospital.

00:08:24.359 --> 00:08:28.040
I want to look at him more carefully, you see.

00:08:28.100 --> 00:08:29.621
Yes, sir.

00:08:29.681 --> 00:08:31.222
I see.

00:08:31.282 --> 00:08:34.603
But how can he get to the hospital?

00:08:34.663 --> 00:08:36.975
It's going to be difficult.

00:08:37.034 --> 00:08:38.775
Why, man?

00:08:38.835 --> 00:08:41.618
The hospital's not far from here.

00:08:41.678 --> 00:08:45.562
Well, yes, sir, I know.

00:08:45.622 --> 00:08:49.944
But you see, Merrick can't walk very well.

00:08:50.004 --> 00:08:52.026
He needs help.

00:08:52.086 --> 00:08:54.668
You can come with him.

00:08:54.728 --> 00:08:56.748
Do you want more money?

00:08:56.808 --> 00:08:58.110
Is that it?

00:08:58.170 --> 00:09:01.562
Well, yes, sir, I do.

00:09:01.622 --> 00:09:05.754
But you see, people are afraid of him, too.

00:09:05.814 --> 00:09:11.456
In the road, little boys always run after him and hit him.

00:09:11.516 --> 00:09:16.106
Then the police get angry because people are afraid.

00:09:16.166 --> 00:09:19.448
Sometimes they take us to prison."

00:09:19.507 --> 00:09:22.118
I see, I said.

00:09:22.178 --> 00:09:25.330
Well, how can he come to the hospital then?

00:09:25.390 --> 00:09:28.661
Bring a cab, sir," said Silcock.

00:09:28.721 --> 00:09:37.406
You can take him to the hospital in a cab.

00:09:37.466 --> 00:09:53.936
CHAPTER II THE CARD So next day, at seven o'clock, I came to the shop in a cab.

00:09:53.996 --> 00:09:59.678
There were not very many people in the road, because it was early in the morning.

00:09:59.738 --> 00:10:06.912
In November it is dark at seven o'clock in the morning, and I could not see the shop very well.

00:10:06.972 --> 00:10:09.233
I waited five minutes.

00:10:09.293 --> 00:10:11.714
A postman walked past.

00:10:11.774 --> 00:10:17.714
Then the door of the shop opened, and the creature, Merrick, came out.

00:10:17.774 --> 00:10:21.346
I could not see his face or his body.

00:10:21.406 --> 00:10:26.467
He had an enormous black hat on his head, like a big box.

00:10:26.527 --> 00:10:31.898
A grey cloth came down from the hat in front of his face.

00:10:31.958 --> 00:10:36.480
There was a hole in the cloth, in front of his eyes.

00:10:36.540 --> 00:10:41.250
He could see out of the hole, but I could not see in.

00:10:41.310 --> 00:10:44.651
He wore a long black coat too.

00:10:44.710 --> 00:10:53.844
The coat began at his neck and ended at his feet, so I could not see his arms, his body or his legs.

00:10:53.904 --> 00:10:58.678
On his feet he wore big shoes like old bags.

00:10:58.738 --> 00:11:03.880
He had a stick in his left hand, and he walked very slowly.

00:11:03.940 --> 00:11:07.742
I opened the door of the cab and got out.

00:11:07.802 --> 00:11:10.958
Good morning, Mr. Merrick, I said.

00:11:11.018 --> 00:11:12.243
Can you get in?

00:11:12.263 --> 00:11:17.714
Oh, my upper steps, he said.

00:11:17.774 --> 00:11:20.275
I'm sorry, I said.

00:11:20.335 --> 00:11:22.705
I don't understand.

00:11:22.765 --> 00:11:28.436
For a minute, he stood by the door of the cab and said nothing.

00:11:28.496 --> 00:11:31.777
Then he hit the cab with his stick.

00:11:31.837 --> 00:11:35.518
Steps, he said loudly.

00:11:35.578 --> 00:11:39.079
Help me up the steps.

00:11:39.140 --> 00:11:42.143
Then I understood.

00:11:42.203 --> 00:11:48.028
There were three steps up into the cab, and he could not get up them.

00:11:48.088 --> 00:11:50.800
Yes, I see.

00:11:50.860 --> 00:11:53.102
I'm sorry, I said.

00:11:53.162 --> 00:11:55.304
Let me help you."

00:11:55.364 --> 00:11:59.738
I took his left hand and began to help him.

00:11:59.798 --> 00:12:03.312
My right hand was behind his back.

00:12:03.372 --> 00:12:05.912
I felt very strange.

00:12:05.972 --> 00:12:13.326
His left hand was like a young woman's, but his back under the coat was horrible.

00:12:13.387 --> 00:12:18.570
I could feel the bags of old skin on his back under the coat.

00:12:18.630 --> 00:12:24.904
He put one enormous foot on the first step, and then he stopped.

00:12:24.964 --> 00:12:29.278
After a minute, he moved his second foot slowly.

00:12:29.338 --> 00:12:31.849
Then he stopped and waited again.

00:12:31.869 --> 00:12:34.931
Hello, sir.

00:12:34.991 --> 00:12:37.094
Can I help you?

00:12:37.154 --> 00:12:39.436
I looked behind me.

00:12:39.496 --> 00:12:45.839
It was the postman, and behind him I could see three young boys.

00:12:45.900 --> 00:12:48.540
One of the boys laughed.

00:12:48.600 --> 00:12:51.532
The postman smiled.

00:12:51.592 --> 00:12:53.934
Is the gentleman ill?

00:12:53.994 --> 00:12:55.464
He asked.

00:12:55.524 --> 00:12:57.555
I thought quickly.

00:12:57.616 --> 00:13:02.618
Yes, but this is a lady, not a gentleman.

00:13:02.678 --> 00:13:05.799
I'm a doctor, and she's ill.

00:13:05.859 --> 00:13:09.749
Take her hand so I can help her better.

00:13:09.809 --> 00:13:17.421
The postman took Merrick's left hand, and I helped him with two hands from behind.

00:13:17.481 --> 00:13:25.094
Slowly, very slowly, Merrick went up the steps and into the cab.

00:13:25.154 --> 00:13:28.524
One boy was very near the cab.

00:13:28.584 --> 00:13:31.226
He called to his friends.

00:13:31.286 --> 00:13:33.830
Come and see this, boys!

00:13:33.890 --> 00:13:36.766
a fat lady in a black coat.

00:13:36.826 --> 00:13:39.696
And look at that enormous hat!"

00:13:39.756 --> 00:13:42.027
The boys laughed.

00:13:42.087 --> 00:13:45.338
They were very near the cab, too, now.

00:13:45.398 --> 00:13:47.408
I closed the door quickly.

00:13:47.428 --> 00:13:51.189
"'Thank you,' I said to the postman.

00:13:51.209 --> 00:13:53.830
"'That's all right, sir,' he said.

00:13:53.850 --> 00:13:57.571
"'She's a strange lady, sir, isn't she?

00:13:57.591 --> 00:13:59.911
"'She's ill.

00:13:59.972 --> 00:14:02.609
That's all,' I said quickly.

00:14:02.669 --> 00:14:04.968
We're going to the hospital.

00:14:05.027 --> 00:14:08.580
Goodbye, and thank you."

00:14:08.640 --> 00:14:13.142
The cab drove down the road to the hospital.

00:14:13.202 --> 00:14:15.574
I looked at Merrick.

00:14:15.634 --> 00:14:18.146
That was difficult, wasn't it?

00:14:18.206 --> 00:14:19.588
I said.

00:14:19.647 --> 00:14:24.430
At first he said nothing, but then he spoke.

00:14:24.490 --> 00:14:32.195
His voice was very strange, but I listened to him carefully, and I could understand him.

00:14:32.255 --> 00:14:38.008
The steps were very difficult, he said.

00:14:38.068 --> 00:14:42.752
But most things are difficult for me.

00:14:42.812 --> 00:14:45.334
Yes, I said.

00:14:45.394 --> 00:14:48.706
Nothing is easy for you, is it?

00:14:48.766 --> 00:14:51.958
No, he said.

00:14:52.018 --> 00:14:55.080
He was very quiet for a minute.

00:14:55.140 --> 00:15:00.704
Then he said, Who are you, sir?

00:15:00.764 --> 00:15:02.953
Who am I?

00:15:03.013 --> 00:15:05.450
Oh, I'm sorry.

00:15:05.510 --> 00:15:08.751
My name is Dr. Treves.

00:15:08.811 --> 00:15:10.111
Here.

00:15:10.171 --> 00:15:12.911
This is my card.

00:15:12.972 --> 00:15:17.012
I gave him a card with my name on.

00:15:17.072 --> 00:15:20.813
Then I thought, that was no good.

00:15:20.873 --> 00:15:23.514
This man can't read.

00:15:23.574 --> 00:15:29.164
But Merrick took the card and looked at it very carefully.

00:15:29.224 --> 00:15:33.410
Then he put it in his trousers pocket.

00:15:33.470 --> 00:15:37.946
I did not talk to him very much at the hospital.

00:15:38.007 --> 00:15:44.931
I looked at his head and arms and legs and body very carefully.

00:15:44.991 --> 00:15:49.964
Then I wrote the important things about him in a little book.

00:15:50.024 --> 00:15:52.586
A nurse helped me.

00:15:52.646 --> 00:15:59.862
Merrick looked at her sometimes, but she did not smile at him or talked to him.

00:15:59.922 --> 00:16:02.604
I think she was afraid of him.

00:16:02.664 --> 00:16:08.470
I think Merrick was afraid too, because he was very quiet.

00:16:08.530 --> 00:16:14.265
At four o'clock I took him back to the shop in a cab.

00:16:14.325 --> 00:16:27.302
The next day I looked in the shop window again, but the picture was not there.

00:16:27.362 --> 00:16:43.872
CHAPTER 3 A LETTER TO THE TIMES I did not see Merrick again for two years.

00:16:43.932 --> 00:16:48.634
Then, one day, the police found him.

00:16:48.694 --> 00:16:55.140
He had my card in his hand, so they brought him to the London hospital.

00:16:55.200 --> 00:17:04.159
He was very tired, hungry, and dirty, so I put him to bed in a quiet little room.

00:17:04.219 --> 00:17:07.474
but he could not stay at the hospital.

00:17:07.534 --> 00:17:13.465
He was not ill, and of course the beds in the hospital offer ill people.

00:17:13.525 --> 00:17:19.166
We have no beds for hungry people or ugly people."

00:17:19.226 --> 00:17:25.948
I told the hospital chairman, Mr. Carr Gong, about Merrick.

00:17:26.008 --> 00:17:34.289
He listened carefully, and then he wrote a letter to the editor of the Times newspaper.

00:17:34.350 --> 00:17:44.396
from the times, December 4, 1886, a letter to the editor.

00:17:44.456 --> 00:17:52.142
Dear sir, I am writing to you about a man in our hospital.

00:17:52.202 --> 00:17:54.724
He needs your help.

00:17:54.784 --> 00:17:59.768
His name is Joseph Merrick, and he is 27 years old.

00:17:59.828 --> 00:18:02.417
He is not ill.

00:18:02.477 --> 00:18:10.832
but he cannot go out of the hospital because he is very, very ugly.

00:18:10.892 --> 00:18:17.617
Nobody likes to look at him, and some people are afraid of him.

00:18:17.677 --> 00:18:22.201
We call him the Elephant Man.

00:18:22.261 --> 00:18:29.988
Two years ago, Merrick lived in a shop near the London Hospital.

00:18:30.048 --> 00:18:36.183
For two pence, People could see him and laugh at him.

00:18:36.244 --> 00:18:48.429
One day, Dr. Frederick Treves, a hospital doctor, saw Merrick, brought him to this hospital and looked at him carefully.

00:18:48.489 --> 00:18:55.422
Dr. Treves could not help Merrick, but he gave him his card.

00:18:55.482 --> 00:19:02.280
Then the shopkeeper, Silcock, took Merrick to Belgium.

00:19:02.340 --> 00:19:06.266
A lot of people in Belgium wanted to see him.

00:19:06.326 --> 00:19:11.538
And so after a year, Merrick had fifty pounds.

00:19:11.598 --> 00:19:21.100
But then Silcock took Merrick's fifty pounds, left Merrick in Belgium, and went back to London.

00:19:21.160 --> 00:19:25.802
Merrick came back to London by himself.

00:19:25.862 --> 00:19:31.808
Everyone on the train and the ship looked at him, and laughed at him.

00:19:31.868 --> 00:19:36.106
In London, the police put him in prison.

00:19:36.166 --> 00:19:43.660
But then they saw Dr. Treaves' card and brought Merrick to the London hospital.

00:19:43.720 --> 00:19:48.782
This man has no money, and he cannot work.

00:19:48.842 --> 00:19:57.186
His face and body are very, very ugly, so of course many people are afraid of him.

00:19:57.246 --> 00:20:00.538
But he is a very interesting man.

00:20:00.598 --> 00:20:05.011
He can read and write, and he thinks a lot.

00:20:05.071 --> 00:20:08.432
He is a good, quiet man.

00:20:08.492 --> 00:20:16.707
Sometimes he makes things with his hands and gives them to the nurses because they are kind to him.

00:20:16.767 --> 00:20:22.040
He remembers his mother, and he has a picture of her.

00:20:22.100 --> 00:20:26.062
She was beautiful and kind, he says.

00:20:26.122 --> 00:20:28.998
But he never sees her now.

00:20:29.058 --> 00:20:34.053
She gave him to Silcock a long time ago.

00:20:34.113 --> 00:20:37.974
Can the readers of the Times help us?

00:20:38.034 --> 00:20:42.965
This man is not ill, but he needs a home.

00:20:43.025 --> 00:20:48.426
We can give him a room at the hospital, but we need some money.

00:20:48.486 --> 00:20:55.842
Please write to me at the London hospital, yours faithfully, F.

00:20:55.902 --> 00:20:56.453
C.

00:20:56.513 --> 00:21:01.858
Carr Gom, chairman of the London Hospital.

00:21:01.918 --> 00:21:07.453
The readers of the Times are very kind, people.

00:21:07.513 --> 00:21:10.356
They gave us a lot of money.

00:21:10.416 --> 00:21:19.554
After one week, we had fifty thousand pounds, so Merrick could live in the hospital for all his life.

00:21:19.615 --> 00:21:25.038
We could give him a home.

00:21:25.098 --> 00:21:38.563
Chapter 4 Merrick's First Home We gave Merrick two rooms at the back of the hospital.

00:21:38.623 --> 00:21:43.894
One room was a bathroom, so he could have a bath every day.

00:21:43.954 --> 00:21:50.736
Soon his skin was much better, and there was no horrible smell.

00:21:50.797 --> 00:21:57.154
The second room had a bed, table and chairs.

00:21:57.214 --> 00:22:02.041
I visited him every day and talked to him.

00:22:02.101 --> 00:22:06.612
He loved reading and talking about books.

00:22:06.673 --> 00:22:15.855
At first he did not know many books, the Bible and one or two newspapers, that's all.

00:22:15.915 --> 00:22:21.846
But I gave him some books of love stories and he liked them very much.

00:22:21.906 --> 00:22:27.570
He read them again and again and talked about them often.

00:22:27.630 --> 00:22:34.125
For him, the men and women in these books were alive, like you and me.

00:22:34.185 --> 00:22:36.866
He was very happy.

00:22:36.926 --> 00:22:41.489
But sometimes, it was difficult for him.

00:22:41.549 --> 00:22:48.702
At first, one or two people in the hospital laughed at Merrick because he was ugly.

00:22:48.762 --> 00:22:53.986
Sometimes, they brought their friends to look at him.

00:22:54.046 --> 00:22:58.564
One day, a new nurse came to the hospital.

00:22:58.624 --> 00:23:01.800
and nobody told her about Merrick.

00:23:01.860 --> 00:23:06.602
She took his food to his room and opened the door.

00:23:06.662 --> 00:23:08.902
Then she saw him.

00:23:08.962 --> 00:23:15.324
She screamed, dropped the food on the floor and ran out of the room.

00:23:15.384 --> 00:23:20.755
I was very angry with the nurse and went to see Merrick.

00:23:20.815 --> 00:23:25.946
He was not happy about it, but he was not very angry.

00:23:26.006 --> 00:23:29.596
I think he felt sorry for the girl.

00:23:29.656 --> 00:23:34.758
People don't like looking at me.

00:23:34.818 --> 00:23:39.732
I know that's Doctor Triebs," he said.

00:23:39.792 --> 00:23:44.446
They usually laugh or scream.

00:23:44.506 --> 00:23:49.680
Well, I don't want nurses to laugh at you, Joseph.

00:23:49.740 --> 00:23:51.642
I said angrily.

00:23:51.702 --> 00:23:54.594
I want them to help you.

00:23:54.654 --> 00:23:59.088
Thank you, Doctor," he said.

00:23:59.148 --> 00:24:02.870
in his strange, slow voice.

00:24:02.930 --> 00:24:06.692
But it's not important.

00:24:06.752 --> 00:24:09.623
Everyone laughs at me.

00:24:09.643 --> 00:24:13.796
I understand that."

00:24:13.856 --> 00:24:16.938
I looked at him sadly.

00:24:16.998 --> 00:24:24.642
In his one good hand, his left hand, he had the little picture of his mother.

00:24:24.702 --> 00:24:27.842
He looked at the picture for a minute.

00:24:27.902 --> 00:24:31.934
and then put it by a flower on the table.

00:24:31.994 --> 00:24:40.872
A tear ran out of his eye and down the skin of his enormous, ugly face.

00:24:40.932 --> 00:24:44.384
"'Dr. Trieves?'

00:24:44.444 --> 00:24:45.745
he said slowly.

00:24:45.765 --> 00:24:55.978
"'You and the nurses are very kind, and I'm very happy here.

00:24:56.038 --> 00:24:59.484
Thank you very much.

00:24:59.544 --> 00:25:15.656
But I know I can't stay here long and I would like to live in a lighthouse after the hospital, please.

00:25:15.716 --> 00:25:20.878
A lighthouse or a home for blind people.

00:25:20.898 --> 00:25:27.152
I think those are the best places for me.

00:25:27.212 --> 00:25:29.312
What do you mean?"

00:25:29.373 --> 00:25:30.744
I asked.

00:25:30.804 --> 00:25:32.754
Why?

00:25:32.814 --> 00:25:35.666
He did not look at me.

00:25:35.726 --> 00:25:41.730
He put the flower on the picture and looked at it carefully.

00:25:41.790 --> 00:25:48.494
Light houses have sea all round them, don't they?

00:25:48.554 --> 00:25:54.872
He said, nobody could look at me in a light house.

00:25:54.932 --> 00:26:08.938
So I would be happy there, and blind people can see nothing, so they couldn't see me, could they?

00:26:08.998 --> 00:26:14.832
But, Joseph, I said, this is your home.

00:26:14.892 --> 00:26:17.634
You live here now.

00:26:17.694 --> 00:26:21.660
You aren't going to leave the hospital.

00:26:21.720 --> 00:26:27.125
Not today, perhaps, he said.

00:26:27.185 --> 00:26:29.536
But soon...

00:26:29.596 --> 00:26:34.988
You are a kind man, Dr. Trieves.

00:26:35.048 --> 00:26:39.180
But I can't stay here very long.

00:26:39.200 --> 00:26:42.622
I have no money.

00:26:42.642 --> 00:26:45.473
I smiled.

00:26:45.533 --> 00:26:48.244
Joseph, I said.

00:26:48.304 --> 00:26:51.054
This is your home now.

00:26:51.115 --> 00:26:53.725
Don't you understand?

00:26:53.785 --> 00:26:58.258
You can stay here all your life."

00:26:58.318 --> 00:27:06.452
Very carefully, I told him about the letter to the Times and the money.

00:27:06.512 --> 00:27:12.946
I don't think he understood at first, so I told him again.

00:27:13.006 --> 00:27:16.438
He was very quiet for a minute.

00:27:16.498 --> 00:27:18.536
Then he stood up.

00:27:18.596 --> 00:27:22.696
and walked up and down the room very quickly.

00:27:22.756 --> 00:27:34.902
A strange sound came from him, like laughing.

00:27:34.962 --> 00:27:52.876
Chapter 5 An important visitor I did not want Merrick to live by himself, like a man in the lighthouse.

00:27:52.936 --> 00:28:03.553
He read his books and talked to me, but I wanted him to talk to more people, and I wanted him to talk to women.

00:28:03.613 --> 00:28:11.368
Merrick read about women in his books, but he did not often talk to women.

00:28:11.428 --> 00:28:17.238
He met the nurses every day, but they did not talk to him very much.

00:28:17.298 --> 00:28:22.974
For them, he was always a creature, not a man.

00:28:23.034 --> 00:28:30.956
One day, one of my friends, a beautiful young woman, came to the hospital.

00:28:31.016 --> 00:28:36.198
I told her about Merrick and took her to his room.

00:28:36.258 --> 00:28:40.688
She opened the door and smiled at him.

00:28:40.749 --> 00:28:44.610
Good morning, Mr. Merrick, she said.

00:28:44.670 --> 00:28:47.390
Then she shook his hand.

00:28:47.450 --> 00:28:52.602
Merrick looked at her for a minute with his mouth open.

00:28:52.662 --> 00:28:59.614
Then he sat down on his bed with his head in his hand and cried.

00:28:59.674 --> 00:29:02.986
He cried for nearly five minutes.

00:29:03.047 --> 00:29:10.340
The tears ran down his face between his fingers and onto the floor.

00:29:10.400 --> 00:29:17.028
My friend sat on the bed beside him and put her hand on his arm.

00:29:17.088 --> 00:29:25.368
She said nothing, but she smiled at him and shook his hand again before she left.

00:29:25.428 --> 00:29:28.890
Dr. Trieves?

00:29:28.950 --> 00:29:31.592
He said to me that night.

00:29:31.652 --> 00:29:36.004
That lady was wonderful.

00:29:36.064 --> 00:29:47.063
My mother smiled at me once, many years ago, but no women smile at me now.

00:29:47.123 --> 00:29:54.778
But this lady smiled at me too, and she shook my hand.

00:29:54.798 --> 00:30:03.320
Her beautiful lady smiled at me and shook my hand.

00:30:03.380 --> 00:30:12.632
My young lady friend came again the next week and talked to Merrick for half an hour.

00:30:12.692 --> 00:30:18.504
Though week after that, she came again with a friend.

00:30:18.564 --> 00:30:23.826
They gave him some books and had a cup of tea with him.

00:30:23.886 --> 00:30:26.676
It was wonderful for him.

00:30:26.736 --> 00:30:31.427
For the first time in his life he had some friends.

00:30:31.487 --> 00:30:34.398
He was a very happy man.

00:30:34.458 --> 00:30:43.229
He sat in his room and read his books and said no more about living on a lighthouse.

00:30:43.289 --> 00:30:51.019
People began to read about Merrick in the newspapers so he had a lot of visitors.

00:30:51.078 --> 00:30:54.240
Everybody wanted to see him.

00:30:54.300 --> 00:30:58.723
A lot of important ladies and gentlemen visited him.

00:30:58.784 --> 00:31:04.577
They smiled at him, shook his hand, and gave him books.

00:31:04.638 --> 00:31:12.142
Merrick liked talking to these people, and he began to forget about his ugly body.

00:31:12.202 --> 00:31:15.786
His visitors never laughed at him.

00:31:15.846 --> 00:31:18.234
He began to feel like a man.

00:31:18.294 --> 00:31:20.822
not a creature.

00:31:20.883 --> 00:31:28.658
One wonderful day, a very important lady came to the hospital to visit him.

00:31:28.718 --> 00:31:33.290
I met the lady and took her to his room.

00:31:33.350 --> 00:31:38.334
Then I opened the door and smiled at him.

00:31:38.394 --> 00:31:42.376
Good morning, Joseph, I said.

00:31:42.436 --> 00:31:49.147
There is a new visitor to see you today, a very famous lady.

00:31:49.207 --> 00:31:53.176
Merrick stood up beside his table.

00:31:53.236 --> 00:32:00.432
He did not smile, because his face could not smile, but his eyes looked happy.

00:32:00.492 --> 00:32:04.406
That's good, he said.

00:32:04.466 --> 00:32:08.098
Who is it?

00:32:08.118 --> 00:32:12.662
I moved away from the door, and the visitor walked in.

00:32:12.722 --> 00:32:18.774
Your Majesty, this is Joseph Merrick, I said.

00:32:18.834 --> 00:32:27.294
Joseph, this is her Majesty, Queen Alexandra, the Queen of England.

00:32:27.355 --> 00:32:31.718
Queen Alexandra smiled at him.

00:32:31.778 --> 00:32:34.679
How do you do, Mr. Merrick?

00:32:34.739 --> 00:32:36.019
She said.

00:32:36.080 --> 00:32:38.991
I'm very pleased to meet you.

00:32:39.052 --> 00:32:42.193
Then she shook his hand.

00:32:42.254 --> 00:32:45.396
Merrick did not move.

00:32:45.456 --> 00:32:48.942
For nearly half a minute he stood.

00:32:49.002 --> 00:32:52.040
and looked at her with his mouth open.

00:32:52.100 --> 00:32:57.884
Then he spoke in his strange, slow voice.

00:32:57.944 --> 00:33:00.566
How?

00:33:00.626 --> 00:33:05.510
How do you do your majesty?

00:33:05.570 --> 00:33:07.132
He said.

00:33:07.192 --> 00:33:15.678
But I don't think the Queen understood him, because he tried to get down on his knees at the same time.

00:33:15.738 --> 00:33:18.650
It was very difficult for him.

00:33:18.710 --> 00:33:21.792
because of his enormous legs.

00:33:21.852 --> 00:33:24.843
No, please, Mr. Merrick.

00:33:24.903 --> 00:33:28.104
Do get up, said the Queen.

00:33:28.164 --> 00:33:30.996
I would like to talk to you.

00:33:31.057 --> 00:33:34.258
Can we sit at your table?

00:33:34.318 --> 00:33:36.459
Yes.

00:33:36.519 --> 00:33:40.521
Yes, of course, he said.

00:33:40.581 --> 00:33:43.442
They sat at the table.

00:33:43.502 --> 00:33:48.737
She took his left hand, the good hand, in hers.

00:33:48.797 --> 00:33:55.354
She looked at the hand carefully and then smiled at Merrick again.

00:33:55.414 --> 00:34:00.998
I often read about you in the newspapers, she said.

00:34:01.058 --> 00:34:05.282
You are a very interesting man, Mr. Merrick.

00:34:05.342 --> 00:34:11.226
You have a very difficult life, but people say you're happy.

00:34:11.287 --> 00:34:13.218
Is it true?

00:34:13.278 --> 00:34:15.979
Are you happy now?

00:34:16.039 --> 00:34:19.819
Oh, yes, your Majesty.

00:34:19.879 --> 00:34:22.800
Yes, said Narig.

00:34:22.860 --> 00:34:25.871
I'm a very happy man.

00:34:25.891 --> 00:34:33.684
I have a home here now, and friends, and my books.

00:34:33.745 --> 00:34:39.256
I'm happy every hour of the day.

00:34:39.316 --> 00:34:43.818
What a wonderful story, she said.

00:34:43.878 --> 00:34:46.755
I'm very pleased to hear it.

00:34:46.816 --> 00:34:51.175
Now, tell me about your reading.

00:34:51.236 --> 00:34:54.178
I see you have a lot of books here.

00:34:54.198 --> 00:34:59.332
Oh, yes, Your Majesty!

00:34:59.393 --> 00:35:02.444
I love my books!"

00:35:02.504 --> 00:35:04.296
said Merrick.

00:35:04.356 --> 00:35:10.922
And for nearly half an hour they sat and talked about books.

00:35:10.982 --> 00:35:14.674
The Queen gave him a little book.

00:35:14.734 --> 00:35:18.874
and some red flowers before she left.

00:35:18.934 --> 00:35:24.658
After her visit, Merrick began to sing.

00:35:24.718 --> 00:35:36.394
He could not sing easily, of course, because of his mouth, but all that day there was a strange, happy noise in his room.

00:35:36.455 --> 00:35:43.068
He looked at the flowers carefully and put them on his table.

00:35:43.128 --> 00:35:52.239
He had many visits from the Queen, and at Christmas she sent him a Christmas card.

00:35:52.299 --> 00:36:00.081
Windsor Castle, the 20th of December, 1888.

00:36:00.141 --> 00:36:06.993
Dear Joseph, here is a small Christmas present for you.

00:36:07.053 --> 00:36:11.054
I think it looks like me, doesn't it?

00:36:11.114 --> 00:36:20.258
I do like visiting you very much, and I am going to come to the hospital again in the new year.

00:36:20.318 --> 00:36:26.802
Happy Christmas, your friend, Alexandra."

00:36:26.862 --> 00:36:33.266
The present was a picture of Queen Alexandra with her name on it.

00:36:33.326 --> 00:36:40.398
Merrick cried over it, and put it carefully by the bed in his room.

00:36:40.458 --> 00:36:45.740
Then he sat down and wrote a letter to the Queen.

00:36:45.801 --> 00:36:50.413
It was the first letter of his life.

00:36:50.473 --> 00:36:59.348
The London Hospital 23rd of December 1888.

00:36:59.408 --> 00:37:11.656
My dear Queen, thank you very, very much for your wonderful card and the beautiful picture.

00:37:11.716 --> 00:37:21.350
It is the best thing in my room, the very best, the most beautiful thing I have.

00:37:21.410 --> 00:37:29.882
This is the first Christmas in my life, and my first Christmas present.

00:37:29.942 --> 00:37:38.335
Perhaps I had a Christmas with my mother once, but I do not remember it.

00:37:38.395 --> 00:37:42.358
I have my mother's picture too.

00:37:42.418 --> 00:37:46.410
and she is beautiful like you.

00:37:46.470 --> 00:37:56.925
But now I know many famous ladies and kind people like Dr. Treves, and I am a very happy man.

00:37:56.945 --> 00:38:05.850
I am happy, too, because I am going to see you in the new year.

00:38:05.910 --> 00:38:11.684
Happy Christmas to you, my dear friend.

00:38:11.745 --> 00:38:22.399
with all my love, Joseph Merrick.

00:38:22.459 --> 00:38:41.550
Chapter 6 Outside the Hospital Merrick had a lot of friends now, but he was more like a child than a man.

00:38:41.610 --> 00:38:50.482
He could read about things and talk to his visitors, but he could not go out of the hospital by himself.

00:38:50.542 --> 00:38:55.036
He thought and played like a child.

00:38:55.096 --> 00:39:00.200
After Christmas, he wanted to go to the theatre.

00:39:00.260 --> 00:39:07.124
This was very difficult because I did not want the people in the theatre to see him.

00:39:07.185 --> 00:39:13.728
But a kind lady from the theatre Mrs. Kendall helped us.

00:39:13.788 --> 00:39:19.242
We bought tickets for a box at the side of the theatre.

00:39:19.302 --> 00:39:29.509
We went to the theatre in a cab with dark windows, and we went into the theatre by a door at the back, the Queen's door.

00:39:29.569 --> 00:39:32.141
Nobody saw us.

00:39:32.201 --> 00:39:40.886
Three nurses sat at the front of the box, and Merrick and I sat in the dark behind them.

00:39:40.946 --> 00:39:47.007
Nobody in the theatre could see us, but we could see the play.

00:39:47.068 --> 00:39:50.439
It was a children's Christmas play.

00:39:50.499 --> 00:39:52.720
Merrick loved it.

00:39:52.780 --> 00:39:56.622
It was a most wonderful, exciting story.

00:39:56.682 --> 00:40:03.735
Often he laughed, and sometimes he tried to sing like the children in the theatre.

00:40:03.795 --> 00:40:06.056
He was like a child.

00:40:06.116 --> 00:40:11.161
For him, everything in the story was true.

00:40:11.222 --> 00:40:19.138
Once he was very afraid, because the bad man in the play was angry and had a knife.

00:40:19.198 --> 00:40:25.230
At first, Merrick wanted to leave the theatre, but I stopped him.

00:40:25.290 --> 00:40:30.472
Then he was very angry with this bad man in the play.

00:40:30.532 --> 00:40:38.764
He hit his hand on his chair and stood up and talked to the man, but nobody heard him.

00:40:38.824 --> 00:40:44.018
When the bad man went to prison, Merrick laughed.

00:40:44.078 --> 00:40:49.620
Merrick thought the beautiful young lady in the play was wonderful.

00:40:49.680 --> 00:40:52.940
He wanted to talk to her, too.

00:40:53.000 --> 00:41:00.622
At the end of the play, he was very happy because she married a good young man.

00:41:00.683 --> 00:41:08.458
He remembered this play for a long time, and he talked a lot about the people in it.

00:41:08.518 --> 00:41:14.375
What do you think they did after we left?"

00:41:14.435 --> 00:41:16.226
he asked me.

00:41:16.286 --> 00:41:21.668
Where do the young lady and the young man live?

00:41:21.728 --> 00:41:24.980
What are they doing now?

00:41:25.040 --> 00:41:27.911
I don't know, I said.

00:41:27.971 --> 00:41:30.912
Perhaps they live in the country.

00:41:30.973 --> 00:41:35.044
Merrick thought about this for a long time.

00:41:35.104 --> 00:41:44.595
Then he said, Dr. Treves, can I go to the country please?

00:41:44.655 --> 00:41:52.828
I saw the country once from a train, but I never went there.

00:41:52.888 --> 00:41:57.470
I often read about it in books.

00:41:57.530 --> 00:42:01.782
It's very beautiful, isn't it?

00:42:01.842 --> 00:42:05.642
I would like to see it.

00:42:05.703 --> 00:42:13.786
The visit to the theatre was difficult, but a visit to the country was more difficult.

00:42:13.846 --> 00:42:18.697
But again one of his new friends helped us.

00:42:18.758 --> 00:42:26.902
She had a small house in the country, and Merrick could stay in it for the summer, she said.

00:42:26.962 --> 00:42:34.589
I took Merrick to the country in a train with dark windows so nobody could see him.

00:42:34.649 --> 00:42:39.086
Then we went in a cab to the country house.

00:42:39.146 --> 00:42:45.929
There were a lot of trees near the house, but no people lived near it.

00:42:45.990 --> 00:42:53.374
A countryman brought food to the house every day, but no people came near it.

00:42:53.434 --> 00:42:56.585
I stayed with him that night.

00:42:56.646 --> 00:43:01.358
At night it was very dark and quiet.

00:43:01.418 --> 00:43:10.280
In the morning, hundreds of birds sang in the trees, and everything outside the house was green.

00:43:10.341 --> 00:43:20.323
Merrick walked under the big trees, looking at things happily and singing his strange song.

00:43:20.383 --> 00:43:26.805
I went back to London, but Merrick stayed there for six weeks.

00:43:26.865 --> 00:43:29.586
He was wonderfully happy.

00:43:29.646 --> 00:43:34.034
Every week He wrote me a letter.

00:43:34.094 --> 00:43:55.934
Apple Tree House West Wickham Berkshire The 21st of July 1889 Dear Doctor Treaves I had a wonderful day again today.

00:43:55.994 --> 00:43:58.436
It was very warm.

00:43:58.496 --> 00:44:04.539
so I walked under the trees and sat by a stream.

00:44:04.599 --> 00:44:11.730
The water in the stream made a beautiful noise, like singing.

00:44:11.790 --> 00:44:14.150
Did you know that?

00:44:14.210 --> 00:44:18.491
I listened to it for two hours.

00:44:18.552 --> 00:44:23.072
Lots of little birds came near me.

00:44:23.132 --> 00:44:28.775
One had a red body in front and a brown back.

00:44:28.835 --> 00:44:34.900
I gave it some bread and it sat on my hand.

00:44:34.960 --> 00:44:39.601
A lot of birds are my friends now.

00:44:39.662 --> 00:44:44.384
I watched the fish in the stream too.

00:44:44.444 --> 00:44:50.967
They were very exciting because they moved very fast.

00:44:51.027 --> 00:44:58.036
One minute they were there and the next minute I couldn't see them.

00:44:58.096 --> 00:45:04.186
but I waited quietly, and they always came back.

00:45:04.246 --> 00:45:10.948
I put my hand in the water, but I couldn't touch them.

00:45:11.008 --> 00:45:14.971
I met a big dog yesterday.

00:45:15.031 --> 00:45:21.524
It made a very loud noise, but I was not afraid.

00:45:21.584 --> 00:45:30.491
I sat down quietly and looked at it, and it came and smelt my hand.

00:45:30.551 --> 00:45:36.282
I saw it again today and gave it some bread.

00:45:36.342 --> 00:45:38.193
It likes me now.

00:45:38.213 --> 00:45:46.135
I am going to put some flowers from the country in this letter.

00:45:46.195 --> 00:45:49.656
There are hundreds of flowers here.

00:45:49.716 --> 00:45:52.156
Did you know that?

00:45:52.216 --> 00:45:56.106
I like the little blue ones best.

00:45:56.167 --> 00:45:59.348
But they are all beautiful.

00:45:59.408 --> 00:46:03.091
I have lots of them in my room.

00:46:03.151 --> 00:46:06.914
I give them water every morning.

00:46:06.974 --> 00:46:10.467
Little flowers are very thirsty, you know.

00:46:10.487 --> 00:46:15.420
I am very happy here, doctor.

00:46:15.480 --> 00:46:26.498
But I want to see you again soon, too, with love from your friend, Joseph Merrick.

00:46:26.558 --> 00:46:32.158
At the end of the summer he came back to London.

00:46:32.218 --> 00:46:37.409
He was very well, and his skin looked much better.

00:46:37.469 --> 00:46:51.234
He talked about the country a lot, but he was happy to see his friends and his books again too.

00:46:51.294 --> 00:47:00.009
the last letter.

00:47:00.069 --> 00:47:09.754
Six months later, in April 1890, I found him dead in bed.

00:47:09.814 --> 00:47:16.178
He was on his back in bed, so at first I thought he was asleep.

00:47:16.238 --> 00:47:20.850
I talked to him, but he did not move.

00:47:20.911 --> 00:47:25.528
Then I saw that the skin on his face was blue.

00:47:25.588 --> 00:47:28.564
so I knew he was dead.

00:47:28.624 --> 00:47:32.266
He did not usually sleep on his back.

00:47:32.326 --> 00:47:42.870
His enormous head was very heavy, so he usually sat up in bed with his arms round his legs and his head on his knees.

00:47:42.930 --> 00:47:50.394
He could sleep well like this, but he wanted to sleep on his back like you and me.

00:47:50.454 --> 00:47:59.566
He tried to sleep on his back that night But his heavy head came off the bed, and he broke his neck.

00:47:59.626 --> 00:48:02.587
He died very quickly.

00:48:02.647 --> 00:48:12.909
Next day, the chairman of the London Hospital, Mr. Carr Gom, wrote to the editor of The Times again.

00:48:12.969 --> 00:48:15.980
The Times, April 16, 1890.

00:48:16.020 --> 00:48:29.772
Dear Sir, Three and a half years ago, I wrote to you about a man called Joseph Merrick.

00:48:29.832 --> 00:48:38.834
This man was called the Elephant Man, because he was born with a very ugly body.

00:48:38.894 --> 00:48:46.426
Merrick was not ill, but he could not work, and he had no money.

00:48:46.486 --> 00:48:50.708
The readers of the Times felt sorry for him.

00:48:50.768 --> 00:48:54.750
and they gave me a lot of money for Merrick.

00:48:54.810 --> 00:49:01.403
Because of this money, we could give Merrick a home in the London Hospital.

00:49:01.463 --> 00:49:09.436
It was his first good home, and for three and a half years, he lived here happily.

00:49:09.496 --> 00:49:17.690
The doctors and nurses of the hospital helped him, and many important people visited him.

00:49:17.750 --> 00:49:20.395
He read many books.

00:49:20.455 --> 00:49:27.851
He went to the theatre, and in the summer he stayed in the country for six weeks.

00:49:27.912 --> 00:49:34.585
Because of your reader's money, we could give him a happy life.

00:49:34.646 --> 00:49:41.699
Last night, Joseph Merrick died quietly in his bed.

00:49:41.760 --> 00:49:48.681
He was a man with a very ugly body, but he was a good, kind man.

00:49:48.742 --> 00:49:51.351
and he had a lot of friends.

00:49:51.412 --> 00:49:57.836
We like to talk to him, and we are all very sorry because he is dead.

00:49:57.896 --> 00:50:03.628
A lot of people are going to remember him for a long time.

00:50:03.688 --> 00:50:09.802
There is some money left, so I am going to give it to the hospital.

00:50:09.862 --> 00:50:15.494
Thank you, sir, for your help.

00:50:15.554 --> 00:50:20.673
Chairman of the London Hospital.

